# Browser
# Gandalf, Goblins' Bane // Flameshape: "Look at the top two cards of your library and exile them face down. For as long as they
# remain exiled, you may play them if you control a Wizard" (CR 406.3, 601.3, 305.1, 611.2). Turn 1: Black Lotus pays for
# Flameshape, which exiles Lightning Bolt and a Plains face down; Bot1 may look at them, Bot2 may not. With no Wizard neither
# can be played - not the Bolt, with {R} floating, nor the Plains, with the land play unused - and the page says what the
# permission waits for. Gandalf himself, cast from exile on his Adventure (CR 715.4), is a Wizard: the Plains is then played as
# the turn's land play, and on turn 3 the Bolt is cast from exile at Bot2. A noncreature spell cast with Gandalf out makes him
# +1/+1 until end of turn and deals 1 damage to each opponent: Bot2 takes 3 and 1. Aerial Doombot, a creature spell, cast on
# turn 1 with Gandalf out, does neither.

